{"lines": ["No distress call. No wreckage. 306 people vanished aboard one US Navy ship.", "March 1918. The collier Cyclops leaves Barbados for Baltimore, carrying manganese ore.", "She is overloaded, one engine broken. Her captain is hated by his crew.", "She never arrives. No lifeboat, no board, no body is ever found.", "At first, the Navy blames German submarines. Germany denies it. Its records show nothing.", "Then rumors of mutiny. The Navy investigates, and finds no evidence of it.", "And that's not the strangest part. In 1941, her two sister ships, Proteus and Nereus, vanish too.", "Same design. Same kind of heavy ore. Both lost without a trace.", "The Navy's best guess: a storm, and a ship built to break. But nobody knows. What do you think happened?"], "words": [["No", 0.0, 0.16], ["distress", 0.16, 0.4], ["call.", 0.4, 0.94], ["No", 1.4, 1.6], ["wreckage.", 1.6, 2.0], ["306", 2.68, 2.92], ["people", 2.92, 3.92], ["vanished", 3.92, 4.26], ["aboard", 4.26, 4.66], ["one", 4.66, 5.1], ["US", 5.1, 5.5], ["Navy", 5.5, 5.92], ["ship.", 5.92, 6.28], ["March", 6.893, 7.04], ["1918.", 7.28, 8.08], ["The", 9.18, 9.26], ["collier", 9.26, 9.68], ["Cyclops", 9.68, 10.2], ["leaves", 10.2, 10.54], ["Barbados", 10.54, 11.32], ["for", 11.32, 11.56], ["Baltimore,", 11.56, 11.86], ["carrying", 12.52, 12.92], ["manganese", 12.92, 13.56], ["ore.", 13.56, 13.84], ["She", 14.43, 14.54], ["is", 14.54, 14.68], ["overloaded,", 14.68, 15.06], ["one", 15.7, 15.9], ["engine", 15.9, 16.3], ["broken.", 16.3, 16.76], ["Her", 17.48, 17.56], ["captain", 17.56, 17.88], ["is", 17.88, 18.14], ["hated", 18.14, 18.42], ["by", 18.42, 18.74], ["his", 18.74, 18.92], ["crew.", 18.92, 19.16], ["She", 19.781, 19.88], ["never", 19.88, 20.06], ["arrives.", 20.06, 20.48], ["No", 21.2, 21.3], ["lifeboat,", 21.3, 21.84], ["no", 22.08, 22.26], ["board,", 22.26, 22.54], ["no", 22.94, 23.04], ["body", 23.04, 23.3], ["is", 23.3, 23.62], ["ever", 23.62, 23.86], ["found.", 23.86, 24.2], ["At", 24.78, 24.86], ["fi